1
00:01:51,157 --> 00:01:54,433
And don't come inside
until the screaming starts.

2
00:03:00,864 --> 00:03:02,864
Sit.

3
00:03:08,674 --> 00:03:10,641
Commune...

4
00:03:10,676 --> 00:03:12,973
or curse?

5
00:03:13,008 --> 00:03:15,844
Curse.

6
00:03:15,879 --> 00:03:19,518
Payment first.

7
00:03:26,054 --> 00:03:28,692
Blood now.

8
00:03:33,699 --> 00:03:35,435
And...

9
00:03:37,263 --> 00:03:39,032
what fate...

10
00:03:41,366 --> 00:03:45,038
for the owner of this blood?

11
00:03:48,406 --> 00:03:52,375
I want the devil himself
to take possession of her,

12
00:03:52,410 --> 00:03:56,346
for both to be locked
in hell together, forever.

13
00:03:57,723 --> 00:04:00,526
Well...

14
00:04:00,561 --> 00:04:03,089
the devil himself

15
00:04:03,124 --> 00:04:07,027
never takes possession.

16
00:04:07,062 --> 00:04:11,702
He sends one of his legions.

17
00:04:11,737 --> 00:04:12,901
A demon?

18
00:04:12,936 --> 00:04:14,540
Mm-hmm.

19
00:04:14,575 --> 00:04:17,543
And it will be
whenever he so chooses,

20
00:04:17,578 --> 00:04:19,710
unless...

21
00:04:21,780 --> 00:04:23,307
What?

22
00:04:24,750 --> 00:04:26,948
It'll cost double.

23
00:04:26,983 --> 00:04:29,214
I'll get it, tonight.

24
00:04:29,249 --> 00:04:31,117
As soon as we finish,

25
00:04:31,152 --> 00:04:34,560
go to this person quickly.

26
00:04:34,595 --> 00:04:38,597
She may be violently ill
and have supernatural strength.

27
00:04:40,832 --> 00:04:42,964
You must take this knife

28
00:04:42,999 --> 00:04:46,968
and wait for the point
of no return,

29
00:04:47,003 --> 00:04:51,137
when the demon has come too far.

30
00:04:51,172 --> 00:04:53,909
How do I know when that is?

31
00:04:53,944 --> 00:04:58,980
You'll see the demon's
three fingers

32
00:04:59,015 --> 00:05:05,591
emerging from the mouth
of the accursed.

33
00:05:05,626 --> 00:05:09,089
Carve a crucifix

34
00:05:09,124 --> 00:05:12,598
into the flesh of the throat,

35
00:05:12,633 --> 00:05:16,602
above the chest.

36
00:05:16,637 --> 00:05:21,299
Are you ready to gaze into hell?

37
00:05:27,010 --> 00:05:28,812
Yes.

38
00:05:45,391 --> 00:05:46,665
Mm.

39
00:05:50,495 --> 00:05:54,200
Come and gaze at his blaze

40
00:05:54,235 --> 00:05:56,972
of fire,

41
00:05:57,007 --> 00:06:03,649
where winged embers rise

42
00:06:03,684 --> 00:06:06,652
to kindling choir!

43
00:06:06,687 --> 00:06:10,480
He is darkness.

44
00:06:10,515 --> 00:06:15,485
He is whispers.

45
00:06:15,520 --> 00:06:19,489
He is sweet

46
00:06:19,524 --> 00:06:24,230
inside your heart.

47
00:06:24,265 --> 00:06:26,837
He is heat.

48
00:06:26,872 --> 00:06:31,237
He is smoke...

49
00:06:32,911 --> 00:06:37,507
...in your throat.

50
00:06:41,920 --> 00:06:43,513
What now?

51
00:06:43,548 --> 00:06:48,089
We wait for the devil
to relight his candle.

52
00:06:48,124 --> 00:06:50,894
Watch close my face,

53
00:06:50,929 --> 00:06:53,699
for the face of the accursed
will soon take mine

54
00:06:53,734 --> 00:06:55,525
but for a moment.

55
00:06:55,560 --> 00:06:58,935
He...

56
00:06:58,970 --> 00:07:01,465
is real.

57
00:07:02,776 --> 00:07:04,941
He...

58
00:07:06,142 --> 00:07:09,275
is imagined.

59
00:07:09,310 --> 00:07:10,914
He...

60
00:07:10,949 --> 00:07:15,545
is stationed at

61
00:07:15,580 --> 00:07:18,053
the seal.

62
00:07:18,088 --> 00:07:19,120
Ahh...

63
00:07:22,587 --> 00:07:24,928
I...

64
00:07:24,963 --> 00:07:27,733
I hear...

65
00:07:27,768 --> 00:07:30,131
a fly.

66
00:07:33,807 --> 00:07:37,303
But I... I don't...

67
00:07:37,338 --> 00:07:39,305
I don't see one.

68
00:07:42,442 --> 00:07:45,949
Do... do you hear it?

69
00:07:48,690 --> 00:07:50,756
Only...

70
00:07:50,791 --> 00:07:52,923
the accursed...

71
00:07:52,958 --> 00:07:55,156
hears the fly!

72
00:08:05,630 --> 00:08:06,970
Where...

73
00:08:07,005 --> 00:08:09,269
did you get...

74
00:08:09,304 --> 00:08:10,468
the blood?!

75
00:08:10,503 --> 00:08:13,273
Where did you get this blood?!

76
00:08:13,308 --> 00:08:16,540
My daughter bled you
while you slept, witch!

77
00:08:20,821 --> 00:08:22,612
My name is Mary Lynn Crandon,

78
00:08:22,647 --> 00:08:25,186
and this is
for my husband Thomas!

79
00:08:45,076 --> 00:08:46,339
Sadie!

80
00:09:14,039 --> 00:09:15,874
Next time we burn it down.

81
00:12:04,044 --> 00:12:07,243
Elly, you need me to stay?

82
00:12:07,278 --> 00:12:09,883
No, you go. I'm fine.

83
00:12:12,118 --> 00:12:13,414
Fine.

84
00:12:15,385 --> 00:12:17,055
Let's go with that.

85
00:12:18,619 --> 00:12:22,027
So, are you going
to stay in town awhile?

86
00:12:22,062 --> 00:12:25,690
Uh... probably
until I sell this place.

87
00:12:25,725 --> 00:12:29,694
I want to get back to Haiti,
they need volunteers.

88
00:12:29,729 --> 00:12:32,235
Lots of junk to clear out,
keep me busy till then.

89
00:12:32,270 --> 00:12:34,237
True.

90
00:12:34,272 --> 00:12:36,701
I can stop by tomorrow,
help you out.

91
00:12:36,736 --> 00:12:38,604
You don't have to do that.

92
00:12:38,639 --> 00:12:40,045
I want to.

93
00:12:40,080 --> 00:12:42,575
I can bring wine,
like old times.

94
00:12:42,610 --> 00:12:44,918
Great. Sounds good.

95
00:12:49,650 --> 00:12:52,090
Hey, Beth?

96
00:12:52,125 --> 00:12:55,225
Thank you
for coming to the service.

97
00:12:55,260 --> 00:12:57,062
It means a lot.

98
00:12:57,097 --> 00:12:58,426
See you tomorrow, El.

99
00:15:52,096 --> 00:15:53,238
Hello?

100
00:15:53,273 --> 00:15:54,404
<i>Hello.</i>

101
00:15:54,439 --> 00:15:56,274
Hey, are you on your way now?

102
00:15:56,309 --> 00:15:59,068
<i>Um, are you in 1952?</i>

103
00:15:59,103 --> 00:16:00,905
<i>Why am I always having to find</i>

104
00:16:00,940 --> 00:16:02,280
<i>a land line number
to call you on?</i>

105
00:16:02,315 --> 00:16:04,645
<i>Like, there is such a thing
as cell phones.</i>

106
00:16:04,680 --> 00:16:06,812
I'm sorry, I'm always losing it.

107
00:16:06,847 --> 00:16:08,913
I've been cleaning nonstop.

108
00:16:08,948 --> 00:16:11,080
<i>Okay, well, since
you don't have a cell phone,</i>

109
00:16:11,115 --> 00:16:12,290
<i>have you seen
your television set,</i>

110
00:16:12,325 --> 00:16:15,084
<i>or is that too much
for you, too?</i>

111
00:16:15,119 --> 00:16:17,427
No. Why?

112
00:16:17,462 --> 00:16:19,264
<i>Oh, shit.</i>

113
00:16:19,299 --> 00:16:22,960
<i>The news, like,
it's pretty rotten.</i>

114
00:16:22,995 --> 00:16:24,434
What's going on?

115
00:16:24,469 --> 00:16:27,305
<i>They're cutting off
all foreign aid to Haiti.</i>

116
00:16:27,340 --> 00:16:31,441
<i>I mean, no one is going
in or out, nobody.</i>

117
00:16:31,476 --> 00:16:33,036
Oh, shit.

118
00:16:34,479 --> 00:16:36,875
<i>Sorry.</i>

119
00:16:40,815 --> 00:16:42,452
So, I called my team leader.

120
00:16:42,487 --> 00:16:43,948
He said
the State Department issued

121
00:16:43,983 --> 00:16:45,950
a level 4 travel advisory.

122
00:16:45,985 --> 00:16:48,194
Level 4, that's bad, right?

123
00:16:48,229 --> 00:16:51,120
Right. It means I can't
get a flight back.

124
00:16:51,155 --> 00:16:53,298
I mean, the worst part is
those people still need help,

125
00:16:53,333 --> 00:16:54,827
and we're just abandoning them.

126
00:16:54,862 --> 00:16:56,466
People need help
here, too, Elly.

127
00:16:56,501 --> 00:16:58,501
We're having a blood drive
at St. Luke's tomorrow.

128
00:16:58,536 --> 00:16:59,997
You could start with that.

129
00:17:00,032 --> 00:17:01,130
Yeah, sign me up.

130
00:17:01,165 --> 00:17:04,133
Really? Now, that is
the Elly I know.

131
00:17:04,168 --> 00:17:05,970
How about we do just
one more of these big boxes

132
00:17:06,005 --> 00:17:07,477
and then pop open
the<i> Vin de Luxe,</i>

133
00:17:07,512 --> 00:17:08,841
- since this is boring.
- Okay.

134
00:17:08,876 --> 00:17:09,908
Yes!

135
00:17:11,714 --> 00:17:12,911
Elly.

136
00:17:15,256 --> 00:17:17,146
Mrs. Dudley, hi.

137
00:17:17,181 --> 00:17:19,148
I'm sorry for your loss.

138
00:17:19,183 --> 00:17:20,721
Thank you.

139
00:17:20,756 --> 00:17:22,360
It's nice of you to stop by.

140
00:17:22,395 --> 00:17:25,990
I only came by to give you back
the spare key.

141
00:17:26,025 --> 00:17:27,497
I...

142
00:17:27,532 --> 00:17:30,368
I'm sorry I wasn't
able to make the service.

143
00:17:30,403 --> 00:17:33,206
It's really all right,
don't worry about it.

144
00:17:34,704 --> 00:17:37,375
Looks like you're busy.

145
00:17:37,410 --> 00:17:39,938
Yeah, we are.

146
00:17:44,879 --> 00:17:47,748
I was the one
who found your mother.

147
00:17:49,422 --> 00:17:51,389
Mrs. Dudley,
do you want to come inside?

148
00:17:51,424 --> 00:17:54,953
I wouldn't have gone inside
if I hadn't heard the music.

149
00:17:56,429 --> 00:17:59,562
Hey, El, where are the boxes
from the attic?

150
00:17:59,597 --> 00:18:01,190
Uh, check the kitchen.

151
00:18:01,225 --> 00:18:04,028
I'm sorry... what music?

152
00:18:04,063 --> 00:18:07,933
That old song she liked
to play, you know the one.

153
00:18:07,968 --> 00:18:11,101
I was passing by on my way
to church when I heard it.

154
00:18:11,136 --> 00:18:12,773
It was a record.

155
00:18:14,238 --> 00:18:16,975
It should have been
skipping, but...

156
00:18:18,583 --> 00:18:19,945
It just...

157
00:18:23,423 --> 00:18:26,050
I just...

158
00:18:26,085 --> 00:18:29,592
Mrs. Dudley, I'm so sorry.

159
00:18:29,627 --> 00:18:31,594
You were always a really great
neighbor to us,

160
00:18:31,629 --> 00:18:33,728
especially after my dad left.

161
00:18:33,763 --> 00:18:35,763
Do you mean when he ran off
with that whore?

162
00:18:37,261 --> 00:18:40,801
Why did you
run off on her, too, Elly?

163
00:18:40,836 --> 00:18:42,605
She was sick.

164
00:18:42,640 --> 00:18:44,772
She had nobody.

165
00:18:44,807 --> 00:18:46,411
If you had been here,

166
00:18:46,446 --> 00:18:48,578
I wouldn't have had
to go through that horror.

167
00:18:48,613 --> 00:18:51,141
I'm sorry for what you saw,
but you have no right

168
00:18:51,176 --> 00:18:53,583
to lecture me about my choices.

169
00:18:53,618 --> 00:18:55,079
Hey! Okay...

170
00:18:55,114 --> 00:18:57,785
I think you'd better
go now, Mrs. Dudley.

171
00:18:59,360 --> 00:19:02,251
I haven't slept for days!

172
00:19:02,286 --> 00:19:05,254
I lie in bed at night.

173
00:19:05,289 --> 00:19:07,630
I keep seeing her face!

174
00:19:10,635 --> 00:19:13,438
I can't believe she slapped me.

175
00:19:13,473 --> 00:19:16,639
No one would believe
that she slapped you.

176
00:19:16,674 --> 00:19:18,641
She's right.

177
00:19:18,676 --> 00:19:20,269
About what?

178
00:19:20,304 --> 00:19:21,842
Maybe I should have been here.

179
00:19:21,877 --> 00:19:24,977
Elly, you were here.
You stuck around.

180
00:19:25,012 --> 00:19:26,880
Yeah, until I didn't.

181
00:19:30,182 --> 00:19:33,854
I hated my dad
after he left her.

182
00:19:33,889 --> 00:19:36,186
Then I did the same thing.

183
00:19:36,221 --> 00:19:41,059
Well, now, your dad walked out
on his wife and his daughter.

184
00:19:42,535 --> 00:19:44,227
That is not at all
the same thing.

185
00:19:45,868 --> 00:19:48,638
All you did was
go out of this town

186
00:19:48,673 --> 00:19:49,969
and went and lived your life.

187
00:19:50,004 --> 00:19:51,476
That's normal, that is healthy.

188
00:19:51,511 --> 00:19:53,874
That is nothing
to feel guilty about.

189
00:19:58,683 --> 00:20:01,486
Shoot, that's my ride.

190
00:20:01,521 --> 00:20:03,345
Should I cancel?

191
00:20:03,380 --> 00:20:05,886
No. No, you've got
an early start.

192
00:20:08,253 --> 00:20:09,494
But I am gonna see you

193
00:20:09,529 --> 00:20:10,990
at the blood drive
tomorrow, right?

194
00:20:11,025 --> 00:20:12,530
- Yes, I'll be there.
- Like seriously.

195
00:20:12,565 --> 00:20:14,158
You're gonna show up,
gonna be there?

196
00:20:14,193 --> 00:20:15,863
- I'm really gonna be there.
- Okay.

197
00:20:17,900 --> 00:20:19,735
You're not your dad

198
00:20:19,770 --> 00:20:23,508
and you're not your mom either.

199
00:20:23,543 --> 00:20:27,842
Okay? You're you,
and you're a good person.

200
00:20:27,877 --> 00:20:29,272
Remember that?

201
00:23:01,096 --> 00:23:03,668
Gamble residence, Elly speaking.

202
00:23:03,703 --> 00:23:05,703
<i>You must be the nurse.</i>

203
00:23:07,267 --> 00:23:08,233
Who's this?

204
00:23:08,268 --> 00:23:10,499
<i>My name is Alma Whitelorn.</i>

205
00:23:10,534 --> 00:23:13,337
<i>I'm calling
on behalf of Ms. Ambrose.</i>

206
00:23:13,372 --> 00:23:15,845
<i>She needs a carer.</i>

207
00:23:15,880 --> 00:23:17,880
<i>Your mother recommended you.</i>

208
00:23:19,543 --> 00:23:21,180
My mother? When?

209
00:23:21,215 --> 00:23:24,447
<i>Last week.
We spoke on the telephone.</i>

210
00:23:27,287 --> 00:23:28,726
I'm sorry...

211
00:23:28,761 --> 00:23:31,190
There must be a mistake.
I've been away.

212
00:23:31,225 --> 00:23:33,357
I only came home
a couple of days ago.

213
00:23:33,392 --> 00:23:35,700
<i>Your mother said you'd be
coming home next week</i>

214
00:23:35,735 --> 00:23:37,262
<i>and to try you then.</i>

215
00:23:37,297 --> 00:23:39,099
<i>Is this a bad time?</i>

216
00:23:47,571 --> 00:23:51,617
Do you think she had it
all planned out?

217
00:23:51,652 --> 00:23:53,916
Um, I don't know.

218
00:23:53,951 --> 00:23:55,082
Maybe.

219
00:23:57,119 --> 00:23:58,624
Ooh.

220
00:23:58,659 --> 00:24:00,417
What happened here?

221
00:24:00,452 --> 00:24:01,924
Oh, um...

222
00:24:03,158 --> 00:24:04,762
Not long after my dad left,

223
00:24:04,797 --> 00:24:06,896
I woke up
in the middle of the night

224
00:24:06,931 --> 00:24:10,460
and... my mom was
sitting there with a syringe

225
00:24:10,495 --> 00:24:12,605
and a little glass vial and...

226
00:24:14,499 --> 00:24:16,070
she took my blood.

227
00:24:16,105 --> 00:24:18,072
Were you sick?

228
00:24:18,107 --> 00:24:20,107
I don't think so.

229
00:24:20,142 --> 00:24:22,274
That's fucked up.

230
00:24:22,309 --> 00:24:25,310
Maybe it's why I became a nurse.

231
00:24:25,345 --> 00:24:30,249
Speaking of you
and your nursing,

232
00:24:30,284 --> 00:24:31,789
you gonna take that job?

233
00:24:31,824 --> 00:24:34,825
I don't know.
I could use the money.

234
00:24:34,860 --> 00:24:37,586
The aid program was helping me
to pay off my nursing school.

235
00:24:37,621 --> 00:24:39,665
I'm been kind of in danger
of defaulting.

236
00:24:39,700 --> 00:24:42,162
What about the sale
of your mom's house?

237
00:24:42,197 --> 00:24:44,626
Turns out she was
in some serious debt.

238
00:24:44,661 --> 00:24:47,772
Okay, well, for once,
I cannot judge your mother,

239
00:24:47,807 --> 00:24:49,972
because we both know
that I know about debt.

240
00:24:51,635 --> 00:24:53,811
But I do think
you should take that job.

241
00:24:53,846 --> 00:24:56,440
The change of scenery
would do you a lot of good.

242
00:24:56,475 --> 00:24:57,947
Yeah. But it's out
in the sticks

243
00:24:57,982 --> 00:24:59,443
and I don't have a car.

244
00:24:59,478 --> 00:25:03,447
Okay, well, as per
my last email, I have a car.

245
00:25:03,482 --> 00:25:05,185
It's a piece of shit,
but it's a car.

246
00:25:05,220 --> 00:25:07,660
I'll drive, you get the gas.

247
00:25:13,558 --> 00:25:16,460
You think she did it
to punish me?

248
00:25:16,495 --> 00:25:17,802
Like trap me?

249
00:25:17,837 --> 00:25:19,804
You're not trapped.

250
00:25:19,839 --> 00:25:22,004
You're gonna sell
that musty old house

251
00:25:22,039 --> 00:25:24,677
and... live your life.

252
00:25:28,749 --> 00:25:30,815
The phone call was so weird.

253
00:25:30,850 --> 00:25:33,477
I don't even know how
my mom knew these people

254
00:25:33,512 --> 00:25:36,920
or... why she recommended me.

255
00:25:38,715 --> 00:25:41,650
<i>There, all done.</i>

256
00:25:49,429 --> 00:25:52,067
Shhh!

257
00:25:52,102 --> 00:25:54,201
Go back to sleep, Eleanor.

258
00:26:55,330 --> 00:26:57,902
<i>Eleanor!</i>

259
00:26:57,937 --> 00:26:59,431
<i>Get in here!</i>

260
00:27:05,769 --> 00:27:07,912
Mother?

261
00:27:07,947 --> 00:27:10,112
<i>Where were you?</i>

262
00:27:10,147 --> 00:27:11,476
I told you, I...

263
00:27:11,511 --> 00:27:14,248
<i>Where... were... you?</i>

264
00:27:14,283 --> 00:27:16,316
I was volunteering...

265
00:28:14,013 --> 00:28:16,145
Look at me!

266
00:28:19,414 --> 00:28:21,018
Do you smell that?

267
00:28:21,053 --> 00:28:23,713
I pissed myself.

268
00:28:23,748 --> 00:28:24,989
And nobody came to help.

269
00:28:25,024 --> 00:28:26,716
Stop!

270
00:28:26,751 --> 00:28:29,895
You should have seen that
nosy old bitch, Mrs. Dudley.

271
00:28:29,930 --> 00:28:31,655
"Help! Somebody, come!"

272
00:28:31,690 --> 00:28:35,164
She just opened up her big
stupid mouth and...

273
00:28:45,704 --> 00:28:47,506
Elly, come on.

274
00:28:47,541 --> 00:28:49,508
It's that crazy neighbor lady,

275
00:28:49,543 --> 00:28:52,676
she just smacked this idea
into your head.

276
00:28:52,711 --> 00:28:54,843
No, it was real.

277
00:28:57,617 --> 00:29:01,751
I mean, it felt real.

278
00:29:02,721 --> 00:29:04,754
Well, maybe you should...

279
00:29:04,789 --> 00:29:06,195
you know.

280
00:29:06,230 --> 00:29:07,933
What?

281
00:29:07,968 --> 00:29:09,429
See someone?

282
00:29:09,464 --> 00:29:12,069
Talk about it, professionally.

283
00:29:12,104 --> 00:29:13,598
Like a psychiatrist?

284
00:29:15,272 --> 00:29:16,403
Yeah, like a...

285
00:29:16,438 --> 00:29:18,405
exactly like a psychiatrist.

286
00:29:18,440 --> 00:29:20,242
Great, then I'll officially
turn into her.

287
00:29:20,277 --> 00:29:23,245
That's not possible, you're
never gonna become your mother.

288
00:29:23,280 --> 00:29:26,281
I'm just...

289
00:29:26,316 --> 00:29:28,547
You're grieving,
and this isn't my line.

290
00:29:28,582 --> 00:29:30,450
I don't know what to do
with this stuff, but...

291
00:29:30,485 --> 00:29:33,420
you can stay with me
for as long as it takes.

292
00:29:53,343 --> 00:29:56,476
Isn't that the record
your mom used to always play?

293
00:29:56,511 --> 00:29:59,149
She always said it was our song.

294
00:29:59,184 --> 00:30:02,086
It was playing
when Mrs. Dudley found her.

295
00:30:02,121 --> 00:30:04,583
Then throw it in a box

296
00:30:04,618 --> 00:30:06,453
or against the wall.

297
00:30:06,488 --> 00:30:08,455
I don't think I can do that.

298
00:30:10,162 --> 00:30:12,096
But I've decided
I'm going to take the job,

299
00:30:12,131 --> 00:30:14,098
if you'll still drive me.

300
00:30:14,133 --> 00:30:18,102
Hey, hey, I am so down
to do anything

301
00:30:18,137 --> 00:30:20,104
that involves us
getting the fuck out of here.

302
00:30:20,139 --> 00:30:21,699
- Okay.
- Okay.

303
00:31:31,936 --> 00:31:33,111
What?

304
00:31:34,609 --> 00:31:36,279
Weirdly familiar.

305
00:31:37,381 --> 00:31:39,381
<i>Take my hand.</i>

306
00:31:46,049 --> 00:31:49,688
Girl, are you, like, 100% sure
you still wanna do this?

307
00:31:49,723 --> 00:31:51,855
This is really
in the middle of nowhere.

308
00:31:51,890 --> 00:31:53,758
Yeah, I'll be fine.

309
00:31:56,598 --> 00:31:58,026
Creepy.

310
00:31:58,061 --> 00:32:01,238
Was she always
standing right there?

311
00:32:04,903 --> 00:32:06,276
Must be Alma.

312
00:32:06,311 --> 00:32:08,905
Yay.

313
00:32:08,940 --> 00:32:10,313
Alma.

314
00:32:15,782 --> 00:32:18,552
Miss Campbell. Hmm.

315
00:32:18,587 --> 00:32:20,785
I'm Alma Whitelorn.

316
00:32:20,820 --> 00:32:23,227
In charge of the Ambrose estate.

317
00:32:23,262 --> 00:32:25,130
We spoke on the telephone.

318
00:32:25,165 --> 00:32:26,626
You're late.

319
00:32:26,661 --> 00:32:28,430
Oh, yeah, sorry.

320
00:32:28,465 --> 00:32:31,565
The drive just took
a bit longer than we expected.

321
00:32:31,600 --> 00:32:33,402
This is my friend Beth.

322
00:32:33,437 --> 00:32:34,799
Hi.

323
00:32:34,834 --> 00:32:36,636
The job's for one person.

324
00:32:36,671 --> 00:32:39,771
Oh, I'm just...
I'm just the driver.

325
00:32:39,806 --> 00:32:43,346
We're a little behind.
If you'll follow me.

326
00:32:45,482 --> 00:32:46,811
Wow.

327
00:32:56,328 --> 00:32:58,262
Refrigerator, oven.

328
00:32:58,297 --> 00:33:00,792
There's no dishwasher
and no microwave.

329
00:33:00,827 --> 00:33:02,629
I'm sure you can make do.

330
00:33:02,664 --> 00:33:03,828
Yeah, no problem.

331
00:33:03,863 --> 00:33:06,666
Help yourself to some fruit.

332
00:33:06,701 --> 00:33:08,272
You can use the fireplace.

333
00:33:08,307 --> 00:33:10,604
The nights have been
growing cold here.

334
00:33:10,639 --> 00:33:12,804
A reliable land line.

335
00:33:12,839 --> 00:33:17,105
You have my phone number
in case of an emergency.

336
00:33:17,140 --> 00:33:19,976
I'll introduce you
to your patient now.

337
00:33:41,901 --> 00:33:43,703
Don't mind if I do.

338
00:33:43,738 --> 00:33:45,969
I made arrangements
for Ms. Ambrose

339
00:33:46,004 --> 00:33:47,344
to have the best possible care,

340
00:33:47,379 --> 00:33:48,972
but they couldn't provide her

341
00:33:49,007 --> 00:33:50,512
with a private room
until Monday.

342
00:33:50,547 --> 00:33:52,976
A bed in a ward
simply wouldn't do.

343
00:33:53,011 --> 00:33:55,143
Ms. Ambrose
is a private woman.

344
00:33:55,178 --> 00:33:57,717
Does she have any family?

345
00:33:57,752 --> 00:33:59,147
A daughter.

346
00:33:59,182 --> 00:34:01,853
But she went away some time ago.

347
00:34:01,888 --> 00:34:03,987
Where did she go?

348
00:34:04,022 --> 00:34:07,364
Your job is Ms. Ambrose.

349
00:34:24,779 --> 00:34:27,351
A precaution, on the off chance

350
00:34:27,386 --> 00:34:29,848
Ms. Ambrose were
to become responsive,

351
00:34:29,883 --> 00:34:31,685
but that won't happen.

352
00:34:31,720 --> 00:34:35,018
However, I must stress that
you do not leave these grounds

353
00:34:35,053 --> 00:34:37,020
until the ambulance arrives
on Monday,

354
00:34:37,055 --> 00:34:40,760
and I won't tolerate
any alcohol on the premises

355
00:34:40,795 --> 00:34:41,926
or any visitors.

356
00:34:41,961 --> 00:34:44,192
Ms. Ambrose is a private...

357
00:34:44,227 --> 00:34:45,798
Private woman? Yeah.

358
00:34:48,605 --> 00:34:50,572
I'll show you to your room now.

359
00:35:23,442 --> 00:35:25,607
Perfect.

360
00:35:25,642 --> 00:35:29,578
I wanted to ask you
about your time volunteering.

361
00:35:29,613 --> 00:35:31,140
Yeah, of course.

362
00:35:31,175 --> 00:35:33,813
Perhaps I misread
the dates on your résumé,

363
00:35:33,848 --> 00:35:35,815
but it seems you were
caring for your mother

364
00:35:35,850 --> 00:35:37,619
at the same time, correct?

365
00:35:39,458 --> 00:35:41,084
Yeah, um...

366
00:35:41,119 --> 00:35:44,087
My experience was
better suited to volunteering...

367
00:35:44,122 --> 00:35:46,958
It's not easy
caring for family, is it?

368
00:35:49,127 --> 00:35:51,765
No, it's not.

369
00:35:51,800 --> 00:35:54,372
So, is this the daughter's room?

370
00:35:55,705 --> 00:35:57,639
There are no other bedrooms.

371
00:35:59,511 --> 00:36:01,104
I really must get going.

372
00:36:01,139 --> 00:36:03,810
If you have any further
questions, I'll see you inside.

373
00:36:09,015 --> 00:36:11,279
She is a real charmer.

374
00:36:11,314 --> 00:36:14,282
Beth, can you
just not say anything else?

375
00:36:14,317 --> 00:36:16,955
Have you met me?

376
00:36:16,990 --> 00:36:19,463
Okay, fine, no problem.
I'll go get some air.

377
00:36:19,498 --> 00:36:21,696
I can't breathe in here, anyway.

378
00:36:21,731 --> 00:36:25,370
Oh, yeah, and I would take
the couch if I were you.

379
00:36:25,405 --> 00:36:26,635
Why?

380
00:36:26,670 --> 00:36:28,032
What if the daughter comes back

381
00:36:28,067 --> 00:36:29,671
and finds Goldilocks in her bed?

382
00:36:48,560 --> 00:36:49,889
How is the apple?

383
00:36:49,924 --> 00:36:51,319
Mm.

384
00:36:51,354 --> 00:36:52,529
Biblical.

385
00:36:54,027 --> 00:36:55,323
She's crazy.

386
00:36:55,358 --> 00:36:56,698
You're fuckin' crazy
for staying.

387
00:36:56,733 --> 00:36:58,931
Well, she's not
gonna stay with me.

388
00:37:00,440 --> 00:37:03,265
Okay,
there she is again. Hello.

389
00:37:04,774 --> 00:37:07,544
Half up front as agreed.
The rest on Monday.

390
00:37:07,579 --> 00:37:09,172
Thank you.

391
00:37:09,207 --> 00:37:10,910
And you'll be leaving soon?

392
00:37:10,945 --> 00:37:13,550
Yep. Right after you do.

393
00:37:17,281 --> 00:37:18,522
Um, Alma.

394
00:37:18,557 --> 00:37:22,955
Do you know how my mother
knew Ms. Ambrose?

395
00:37:25,564 --> 00:37:28,532
I believe they were
old acquaintances, no?

396
00:37:28,567 --> 00:37:30,094
Uh... maybe.

397
00:37:30,129 --> 00:37:32,063
I'm not really sure.

398
00:37:32,098 --> 00:37:34,901
Well, if that's all,
I'll say good afternoon then.

399
00:37:36,476 --> 00:37:37,904
Thanks for everything.

400
00:37:41,404 --> 00:37:43,206
Yeah, I rest my case.

401
00:37:55,990 --> 00:37:57,561
All right, get it all out.

402
00:37:57,596 --> 00:38:00,223
Okay, for openers,
you don't have a car.

403
00:38:00,258 --> 00:38:01,895
That's why you drove me.

404
00:38:01,930 --> 00:38:03,567
Which is exactly how I know
you don't have a car.

405
00:38:03,602 --> 00:38:05,965
Also, you barely know
how to use a cell phone,

406
00:38:06,000 --> 00:38:07,395
so, what if something happens?

407
00:38:07,430 --> 00:38:09,804
You're in the middle of nowhere.

408
00:38:09,839 --> 00:38:11,476
You would be literally stranded.

409
00:38:11,511 --> 00:38:12,972
I'm looking
after a comatose woman

410
00:38:13,007 --> 00:38:14,809
in a country cabin.

411
00:38:14,844 --> 00:38:17,405
I mean, look at this place,
it's like an Airbnb.

412
00:38:17,440 --> 00:38:19,649
Yeah, super nice Airbnb,

413
00:38:19,684 --> 00:38:22,311
even comes with its own
little check-in receptionist

414
00:38:22,346 --> 00:38:24,148
who's also married to Satan.

415
00:38:24,183 --> 00:38:25,787
And then the host
stays with you in a coma.

416
00:38:25,822 --> 00:38:27,415
Five-star review.

417
00:38:27,450 --> 00:38:29,791
You're the one who talked me
into taking this job.

418
00:38:29,826 --> 00:38:31,991
Yeah, because I thought you
needed a change of scenery.

419
00:38:32,026 --> 00:38:34,125
- Yeah, this is it.
- That's not what I meant.

420
00:38:34,160 --> 00:38:35,764
- Alma's gone now.
- Could you just stop?

421
00:38:35,799 --> 00:38:37,458
Shut up, just stop!

422
00:38:37,493 --> 00:38:39,801
Look me in the eye and tell me
you're not taking this job

423
00:38:39,836 --> 00:38:41,264
just because
of you and your mom,

424
00:38:41,299 --> 00:38:43,167
'cause there are
a lot of similarities here

425
00:38:43,202 --> 00:38:44,806
I can't ignore.

426
00:38:47,844 --> 00:38:50,273
Listen, I'm staying.

427
00:38:50,308 --> 00:38:52,979
And I would really appreciate
your support on this.

428
00:38:55,654 --> 00:38:57,280
Okay, fine.

429
00:38:57,315 --> 00:38:59,623
Better give me your land line
because you and phones...

430
00:38:59,658 --> 00:39:01,119
I already texted it to you.

431
00:39:01,154 --> 00:39:04,485
Oh, you do know how
to use a cell phone.

432
00:39:04,520 --> 00:39:08,027
Look at you, going
into the 21st century.

433
00:39:08,062 --> 00:39:10,194
I'm proud of you.
You're fuckin' insane.

434
00:39:10,229 --> 00:39:11,998
- Really sweet, thank you.
- Yeah, I know.

435
00:39:12,033 --> 00:39:13,802
I love you too, bitch.

436
00:40:15,558 --> 00:40:17,734
Ms. Ambrose, my name is Elly.

437
00:40:17,769 --> 00:40:20,363
Now, I understand
you like your privacy

438
00:40:20,398 --> 00:40:23,069
and I respect that,
but if you need anything,

439
00:40:23,104 --> 00:40:25,071
day or night,
don't hesitate to call me.

440
00:40:25,106 --> 00:40:26,941
I'll be here.

441
00:40:29,077 --> 00:40:31,374
Okay, so I'm just going

442
00:40:31,409 --> 00:40:33,585
to pull the covers down here.

443
00:40:39,087 --> 00:40:43,661
Make sure you're nice
and tight... there.

444
00:40:53,596 --> 00:40:55,134
Ms. Ambrose.

445
00:40:55,169 --> 00:40:56,938
Hello, how are you?

446
00:41:34,340 --> 00:41:35,647
<i>Eleanor!</i>

447
00:41:37,849 --> 00:41:39,211
<i>Get in here!</i>

448
00:43:23,251 --> 00:43:26,923
And no microwave.

449
00:43:41,269 --> 00:43:43,137
<i>Eleanor!</i>

450
00:43:48,474 --> 00:43:49,781
<i>Eleanor!</i>

451
00:46:43,451 --> 00:46:45,616
Hi, Ms. Ambrose.

452
00:46:49,523 --> 00:46:52,964
Just gonna check
your pulse here, okay?

453
00:46:54,957 --> 00:46:57,298
Blue's a good color for you.

454
00:46:57,333 --> 00:46:59,300
I'm sure you know that.

455
00:47:00,534 --> 00:47:01,929
All good.

456
00:47:01,964 --> 00:47:04,041
I think you look ready
for bed, huh?

457
00:47:05,803 --> 00:47:07,143
Me too.

458
00:47:08,707 --> 00:47:10,773
I'll just, uh...

459
00:47:10,808 --> 00:47:12,940
sit with you for a little while.

460
00:48:29,722 --> 00:48:31,194
Hello. Ambrose residence.

461
00:48:31,229 --> 00:48:33,394
<i>Hello, Nurse Gamble.</i>

462
00:48:33,429 --> 00:48:34,923
Hey, what's up?

463
00:48:34,958 --> 00:48:36,397
<i>Just thought I'd call
and check in.</i>

464
00:48:36,432 --> 00:48:38,058
<i>Tried your cell, but per usual,</i>

465
00:48:38,093 --> 00:48:40,203
<i>you threw it in the middle
of the ocean somewhere.</i>

466
00:48:40,238 --> 00:48:41,930
Sorry, I was sitting
with Ms. Ambrose

467
00:48:41,965 --> 00:48:43,030
and I had some music playing.

468
00:48:43,065 --> 00:48:45,604
<i>Oh, it sounds romantic.</i>

469
00:48:45,639 --> 00:48:47,870
Not exactly, you weirdo.

470
00:48:47,905 --> 00:48:49,872
Oh, so I found some old records,

471
00:48:49,907 --> 00:48:51,445
and they all had
"Dorothy Ambrose"

472
00:48:51,480 --> 00:48:53,447
written on them...
I guess that's the daughter?

473
00:48:53,482 --> 00:48:57,220
<i>You mean the one that
went away some time ago?</i>

474
00:48:57,255 --> 00:48:59,255
Do you really think
she'll come back?

475
00:48:59,290 --> 00:49:01,048
<i>Okay, are you having
a delayed freakout?</i>

476
00:49:01,083 --> 00:49:02,588
<i>'Cause I can
still come and get you.</i>

477
00:49:02,623 --> 00:49:03,886
No, I'm fine.

478
00:49:03,921 --> 00:49:05,228
Thank you for
the vote of confidence.

479
00:49:05,263 --> 00:49:07,054
<i>Listen, it turns out
that I'm off Sunday,</i>

480
00:49:07,089 --> 00:49:09,056
<i>so how about I come down there,</i>

481
00:49:09,091 --> 00:49:11,564
<i>bring you some real food,
perhaps some real booze?</i>

482
00:49:11,599 --> 00:49:14,732
I mean, that does
sound tempting.

483
00:49:14,767 --> 00:49:16,063
Don't know what I'm gonna do

484
00:49:16,098 --> 00:49:18,065
with all these
microwave dinners.

485
00:49:18,100 --> 00:49:19,803
<i>Eleanor.</i>

486
00:49:21,103 --> 00:49:22,179
<i>Elly?</i>

487
00:49:25,844 --> 00:49:27,250
Yeah?

488
00:49:27,285 --> 00:49:29,120
<i>What is it?</i>

489
00:49:30,486 --> 00:49:32,079
Um... nothing.

490
00:49:32,114 --> 00:49:33,454
But I should go.

491
00:49:33,489 --> 00:49:36,083
<i>Okay, just...
look out for yourself, okay?</i>

492
00:49:36,118 --> 00:49:38,426
Yes, nurse.
I'll see you Sunday.

493
00:49:38,461 --> 00:49:39,460
<i>Night.</i>

494
00:49:39,495 --> 00:49:40,692
Night.

495
00:50:42,085 --> 00:50:44,888
Looks like someone's trying
to scare you is all.

496
00:50:44,923 --> 00:50:46,153
Well, they succeeded.

497
00:50:46,188 --> 00:50:47,330
I'll look into it,

498
00:50:47,365 --> 00:50:49,365
but I don't think
you need to worry, ma'am.

499
00:50:49,400 --> 00:50:51,367
It's probably some kids.

500
00:50:51,402 --> 00:50:52,863
Do kids even live around here?

501
00:50:52,898 --> 00:50:54,997
It just feels pretty isolated.

502
00:50:55,032 --> 00:50:57,373
Yeah, you're right about that,
it is isolated.

503
00:50:57,408 --> 00:51:00,002
But there's some farmland
that borders the property.

504
00:51:00,037 --> 00:51:03,247
I'll ask around and see
if anybody saw anything.

505
00:51:03,282 --> 00:51:04,677
Okay.

506
00:51:04,712 --> 00:51:07,075
The place has a bit
of a history is all.

507
00:51:08,210 --> 00:51:09,583
A history of...?

508
00:51:09,618 --> 00:51:11,684
It's superstitious stuff

509
00:51:11,719 --> 00:51:13,950
that people like you and me
pay no attention to.

510
00:51:15,723 --> 00:51:17,756
But I'll check back in
if I find anything.

511
00:51:17,791 --> 00:51:19,362
How long you planning
on sticking around for?

512
00:51:19,397 --> 00:51:21,595
Just until Monday.
An ambulance is gonna come

513
00:51:21,630 --> 00:51:23,190
take Ms. Ambrose
to the hospital.

514
00:51:23,225 --> 00:51:24,565
Dorothy took ill?

515
00:51:24,600 --> 00:51:27,469
No, Dorothy's away.
I'm looking after her mother.

516
00:51:29,231 --> 00:51:31,374
Old Ms. Ambrose?

517
00:51:31,409 --> 00:51:33,574
Yeah, that's right.

518
00:51:36,238 --> 00:51:38,414
I thought she died.

519
00:51:38,449 --> 00:51:39,712
Oh, no.

520
00:51:39,747 --> 00:51:40,779
Well, she had a stroke,

521
00:51:40,814 --> 00:51:43,419
but... still hanging in there.

522
00:51:49,592 --> 00:51:50,954
All right.

523
00:51:52,254 --> 00:51:53,561
Well, I better get going.

524
00:51:53,596 --> 00:51:55,222
Yeah.

525
00:51:55,257 --> 00:51:57,257
- Good night, ma'am.
- Thank you for coming.

526
00:51:57,292 --> 00:51:58,764
Oh, any time.
Have a good night.

527
00:51:58,799 --> 00:51:59,831
Good night.

528
00:53:14,677 --> 00:53:16,479
Hey.

529
00:53:16,514 --> 00:53:18,074
What's your name?

530
00:53:20,342 --> 00:53:21,880
My name's Elly.

531
00:53:21,915 --> 00:53:23,420
You live around here?

532
