785
01:18:30,191 --> 01:18:32,818
I thought you said she was dead.

786
01:18:32,853 --> 01:18:34,820
We need to leave now.

787
01:18:34,855 --> 01:18:36,657
I'm not leaving
some old sick woman

788
01:18:36,692 --> 01:18:38,560
to be burnt up in her bed
by some nut.

789
01:18:38,595 --> 01:18:41,662
Look, you can't go back there.

790
01:18:41,697 --> 01:18:44,874
You can wait out front
with my partner if you like.

791
01:18:47,703 --> 01:18:48,834
Fuck!

792
01:18:48,869 --> 01:18:52,013
Officer Green,
don't go in there!

793
01:18:52,048 --> 01:18:54,048
Just wait outside.

794
01:18:57,955 --> 01:18:59,845
Ms. Ambrose?

795
01:18:59,880 --> 01:19:02,221
Ma'am, are you in here?

796
01:19:04,258 --> 01:19:06,060
Oh!

797
01:19:28,909 --> 01:19:31,382
- Open up!
- Back away from the door!

798
01:19:31,417 --> 01:19:32,713
Get out of there now!

799
01:19:32,748 --> 01:19:34,880
Step away from the door!

800
01:19:34,915 --> 01:19:37,454
She's not human,
you have to get out!

801
01:19:37,489 --> 01:19:38,884
Officer Green, please!

802
01:19:38,919 --> 01:19:41,260
Please listen to me,
I was set up!

803
01:19:41,295 --> 01:19:44,098
- You have got to get out!
- Please! Please!

804
01:19:44,133 --> 01:19:46,727
Just listen to me,
you have to listen to me.

805
01:19:46,762 --> 01:19:48,399
You have to get out now!

806
01:19:50,667 --> 01:19:55,472
Officer Green, open the door
right now!

807
01:19:55,507 --> 01:19:56,737
Please!

808
01:19:58,312 --> 01:19:59,905
Please!

809
01:19:59,940 --> 01:20:01,907
What the fuck?

810
01:20:12,821 --> 01:20:14,326
Officer Green?

811
01:20:36,812 --> 01:20:38,647
Help!

812
01:20:40,552 --> 01:20:42,948
- Officer!
- What happened to you?

813
01:20:42,983 --> 01:20:44,653
Uh... It's a long story.

814
01:20:44,688 --> 01:20:46,787
Wait, where is my partner?

815
01:20:46,822 --> 01:20:47,788
She killed him.

816
01:20:47,823 --> 01:20:49,361
- Who?
- Ms. Ambrose.

817
01:20:49,396 --> 01:20:51,495
I need to find out
what the hell's going on here.

818
01:20:51,530 --> 01:20:52,727
Get in that house...

819
01:21:01,903 --> 01:21:04,013
Beth?

820
01:21:07,007 --> 01:21:09,975
Oh, Beth. Oh, my God.

821
01:21:10,010 --> 01:21:11,350
It's gonna be okay.

822
01:21:25,762 --> 01:21:28,103
I'm so tired.

823
01:21:49,049 --> 01:21:51,126
Alma? What did you do?

824
01:22:10,411 --> 01:22:12,037
Alma, please...

825
01:22:12,072 --> 01:22:13,544
<i>Now, hush.</i>

826
01:22:13,579 --> 01:22:15,579
<i>This won't hurt a bit, Eleanor.</i>

827
01:22:18,617 --> 01:22:20,914
<i>Everything's gonna be okay.</i>

828
01:22:23,589 --> 01:22:25,424
There, there.

829
01:22:25,459 --> 01:22:27,558
All done.

830
01:22:27,593 --> 01:22:29,054
Where is she?

831
01:22:29,089 --> 01:22:31,265
Shh!

832
01:22:31,300 --> 01:22:34,235
Your mother brought you here
a long time ago.

833
01:22:34,270 --> 01:22:36,963
You were just a girl.

834
01:22:36,998 --> 01:22:39,570
I gave you an apple.

835
01:22:39,605 --> 01:22:42,639
She wanted to put a curse
on your deadbeat daddy,

836
01:22:42,674 --> 01:22:44,905
but she didn't have
any money to pay with,

837
01:22:44,940 --> 01:22:46,247
so she paid in blood.

838
01:22:46,282 --> 01:22:48,073
Your blood, Elly.

839
01:22:48,108 --> 01:22:50,075
A curse for a curse.

840
01:22:50,110 --> 01:22:51,747
My mother stored it
in the cellar

841
01:22:51,782 --> 01:22:53,254
in case she'd ever need it,

842
01:22:53,289 --> 01:22:54,915
but you destroyed it tonight,

843
01:22:54,950 --> 01:22:56,851
and now I'm calling in the debt.

844
01:22:59,856 --> 01:23:02,989
You're out of your fucking mind.

845
01:23:04,630 --> 01:23:07,092
Your mother always knew
this day would come.

846
01:23:07,127 --> 01:23:09,666
That's why she came back.

847
01:23:09,701 --> 01:23:13,098
That's why she hanged herself,

848
01:23:13,133 --> 01:23:14,275
to offer you up.

849
01:23:14,310 --> 01:23:16,134
It's your fate, Elly.

850
01:23:16,169 --> 01:23:20,380
Then why did you have to kill
Beth, you psycho bitch?

851
01:23:30,986 --> 01:23:32,524
It's a catchy song.

852
01:23:32,559 --> 01:23:34,625
I can see why
you hum it all the time.

853
01:23:35,991 --> 01:23:38,662
Wait, wait, wait! Wait.

854
01:23:38,697 --> 01:23:42,127
Dorothy... I know you're
Ms. Ambrose's daughter.

855
01:23:42,162 --> 01:23:44,338
You don't
have to pretend anymore.

856
01:23:44,373 --> 01:23:46,505
I get what it's like
to look after a sick parent.

857
01:23:46,540 --> 01:23:48,133
You were right, it's not easy.

858
01:23:48,168 --> 01:23:50,806
Believe me, I know.

859
01:23:50,841 --> 01:23:53,974
Listen, Mary Lynn
told me everything.

860
01:23:54,009 --> 01:23:57,318
I don't blame you
for running away.

861
01:23:57,353 --> 01:23:58,814
Fuck.

862
01:23:58,849 --> 01:24:00,882
I lied to you about
why I was volunteering.

863
01:24:00,917 --> 01:24:03,148
I couldn't handle
looking after my mother.

864
01:24:03,183 --> 01:24:05,491
I was scared of her, I was
scared of turning into her,

865
01:24:05,526 --> 01:24:08,362
so I ran way, just like my dad.

866
01:24:10,399 --> 01:24:11,860
I left her

867
01:24:11,895 --> 01:24:15,501
when she needed me most.

868
01:24:15,536 --> 01:24:17,536
And she killed herself.

869
01:24:19,375 --> 01:24:21,540
I know your pain, Dorothy.

870
01:24:24,710 --> 01:24:27,678
My name is Alma.

871
01:24:45,093 --> 01:24:48,270
There's your friend.

872
01:24:48,305 --> 01:24:49,568
In your face!

873
01:24:49,603 --> 01:24:52,032
Always had an answer
for everything!

874
01:24:52,067 --> 01:24:53,935
Well, I fooled her, didn't I?

875
01:24:55,609 --> 01:24:57,774
Now, swallow her down!

876
01:25:08,281 --> 01:25:10,952
This is a ritual
my mother taught me.

877
01:25:15,827 --> 01:25:17,563
Are you ready...

878
01:25:17,598 --> 01:25:19,829
to gaze into hell?

879
01:25:35,616 --> 01:25:38,419
"Come and gaze
at his blaze of fire,

880
01:25:38,454 --> 01:25:42,423
where winged embers rise
to kindling choir!"

881
01:25:42,458 --> 01:25:45,085
"He is darkness, he is whispers,

882
01:25:45,120 --> 01:25:47,593
he is sweet inside
your heart."

883
01:25:47,628 --> 01:25:50,431
"He is heat, he is smoke,

884
01:25:50,466 --> 01:25:52,928
he is fire in your throat."

885
01:25:52,963 --> 01:25:55,293
Ms. Ambrose?

886
01:25:55,328 --> 01:25:57,834
"I invite you
to rise out of your shell."

887
01:25:57,869 --> 01:26:02,476
"I implore you
to visit us from hell."

888
01:26:04,810 --> 01:26:08,009
He is coming
for his fresh vessel!

889
01:26:14,391 --> 01:26:16,853
Yes!

890
01:26:19,319 --> 01:26:20,329
No...

891
01:26:22,190 --> 01:26:23,695
What's happening?

892
01:26:25,897 --> 01:26:27,963
No...

893
01:26:27,998 --> 01:26:31,032
What's happening to her?

894
01:26:50,526 --> 01:26:51,657
Take her!

895
01:26:54,761 --> 01:26:55,892
You!

896
01:26:58,358 --> 01:26:59,731
Curse you!

897
01:27:02,538 --> 01:27:04,703
You tried that already.

898
01:27:37,430 --> 01:27:40,365
"Demon, O Demon,
take back now to part

899
01:27:40,400 --> 01:27:42,939
well of flame
that floods the heart."

900
01:27:42,974 --> 01:27:46,107
"Demon, O Demon,
return to thine host,

901
01:27:46,142 --> 01:27:49,275
rejoin thine legion,
abandon this host!"

902
01:27:49,310 --> 01:27:51,211
"Retreat now, O Dark One."

903
01:27:51,246 --> 01:27:53,279
"Scatter your ashes
to the winds."

904
01:27:53,314 --> 01:27:56,084
"He's brightness, he's singing,

905
01:27:56,119 --> 01:27:58,086
he's the balance
for the blood."

906
01:28:00,123 --> 01:28:02,728
"He is ice, he is pain,

907
01:28:02,763 --> 01:28:05,225
he is lightning,
and he is rain."

908
01:28:51,207 --> 01:28:52,811
Let's go!

909
01:29:04,055 --> 01:29:06,990
<i>Eleanor!</i>

910
01:29:07,025 --> 01:29:08,497
<i>Don't leave me!</i>

911
01:30:36,576 --> 01:30:38,213
Hey, Elly, I'm gonna
grab a coffee.

912
01:30:38,248 --> 01:30:40,919
- Want anything?
- I'm okay, thank you.

